  "articleBody": "It's easy to get excited about finishing your basement, but watch out for these common finish carpentry pitfalls! One big mistake is under-specifying the details. You've got to be super clear about the look you're going for, right down to the type of trim and how it connects. Another common issue is not clarifying who's supplying the finish materials. This can lead to delays or unexpected costs if you're not on the same page with your contractor. And, honestly, choosing a bid that seems too good to be true often means they've left out crucial scope items, like scribing, custom cuts, or those all-important post-install touch-ups. When you're looking for someone to do the work, ask for references from recent jobs and check for clear documentation of what's included. A skilled carpenter, like the team at HH Remodeling LLC, will make sure these intricate details are covered, especially when dealing with the unique challenges of basement spaces. They'll ensure your project meets your expectations, avoiding those visible measurement errors that can really stand out in finish work. Don't let these mistakes derail your dream basement!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
